   "install": {
    "title": "Installation",
    "html": "<h5>Quick start</h5>\n<p>Scaffold a project with the server, worker, admin dashboard and GraphQL APIs ready to run:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @vendure/create my-shop\n</code></pre>\n<p>Requires Node.js 22.12+ (20.19+ still runs, but Node.js 20 is end-of-life) and a SQL database (PostgreSQL, MySQL, MariaDB or SQLite). The <a href=\"https://docs.vendure.io/guides/getting-started/installation/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">getting started guide</a> covers configuration, seed data and your first plugin. Ask questions on <a href=\"https://vendure.io/discord\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">our Discord</a>.</p>\n<h5>Self-hosting</h5>\n<p>Vendure runs anywhere Node.js runs, including Docker, Kubernetes, a single VM or any cloud provider. Self-hosting is free, and your data stays in your own database. See the <a href=\"https://docs.vendure.io/guides/deployment/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">deployment guides</a>.</p>\n<h5>Vendure Cloud</h5>\n<p><a href=\"https://vendure.io/cloud\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Vendure Cloud</a> is the managed runtime for Vendure. It deploys on git push, creates a preview environment for every pull request, and manages the database, queues, search, backups and scaling. It runs the same application you can self-host, so you can move to Cloud without rebuilding it. Every paid plan includes Cloud at no extra cost. Cloud is in design-partner preview now, with general availability planned for Q1 2027.</p>\n<br />",
    "truncated": false,
